  "id": "p200",
  "term": "P200",
  "definition": "P200 is an electrophysiological brain response measure in which the size of the P200 wave can change with cognitive training. In this study, larger P200 amplitudes during a trained visuospatial working-memory task were taken as a sign of task-specific learning and neural modulation.",
